 			goto out;
 		}
```
Reason:  
The `restore_reserve_on_error()` function properly reverts the per-VMA reservation state (i.e., marks the reservation as unused again) before freeing the folio. This ensures that the reservation is not leaked after a failed copy. The call is added immediately before `folio_put()` on both error paths, matching the pattern already used elsewhere (e.g., in the same function for the `copy_folio_from_user` fallback).

